Mike Stubblefield wrote:
> 

> VOLUME DATA SUMMARY FOR DUB0: Cannot be found. /image cannot be used.
> 
> HELPPPPPP
> 
> There has to be a way to place VMS on a blank disk... I remember it somewhere
> but my mind is so bad these days...

You can put VMS on a blank disk, but not with *that* backup tape.  It
was apparently not created with the /IMAGE qualifier, which is an
_absolute_ necessity for system disk backups.  What that error message
is telling you is that the backup operation that created that tape did
not save the volume initialization information from the disk that was
backed up, most likely due to the omission of the /IMAGE qualifier.
 
> Any help you guys can give me I will appreciate as much as I have the help in
> the past...

If you can make a new backup of the source system disk, do so, and be
sure to use /IMAGE.  Beyond that, you're stuck.

