jasmeer@informix.com (J. A. Jasmeer) writes...
}%MACRO64-F-INSVIRMEM, Virtual memory exhausted after assembling 112512 lines.
} 
}I tried to fix this problem by increasing the swap file and the page file. But
}the system gives the same error message asfter assembling 112512 lines.
}Prakasan.

You need to make sure that the process that is doing the build can acutally
use the virtual memory.  Check the process quotas, particularly the pageing
file quota (Pgflquo) which sets the upper limit for the process (from
the HELP MOD /PGFLQUOTA within the authorize utility: "This is the maximum
number of pages that the person's process can use in the system paging file.")
and while you are there check the working set limits, especially the
extent (WSextent).  You also need to check the VIRTUALPAGECNT system parameter
via sysgen - MCR SYSGEN SHOW VIRTUALPAGECNT will show you what it is set to
(this parameter sets the total number of pages/pagelets a process can map,
if it is lower than the process quota it wins and the process is limited
to this size). Change it by putting an appropriate entry in
SYS$SYSTEM:MODPARAMS.DAT (removing any inappropriate entries from that file
while you're there), an entry like "MIN_VIRTUALPAGECNT = 200000" or whatever
would be the way to go. Then run autogen with a reboot to set the parameter
(since it isn't dynamic so it requires a reboot) as with an
"@sys$update:autogen savparams reboot".

There, I've taken my turn answering this sort of thing...  Is this "I'm out
of virtual memory, how do I get more?" in the FAQ anywhere?

--- Carl



