If you are running VMS V6.1 or V6.2 there could be a problem with the SYSGEN 
parameters:
	PQL_MWSDEFAULT
	PQL_MWSEXTENT
There is a bug in AUTOGEN which sets those paramaters to WSMAX.
So almost every process on the system can grow to wsmax, because when created
a process it allways takes for WSEXTENT the maximum of PQL_MWSEXTENT and what's 
defined in SYSUAF or the WSEXTENT of the batch queue.
On my system i got a lot of problems all regarding to memory,virtual memory, 
etc.
You got more problems if the WSMAX on your system in higher than normal.

In AUTOGEN.COM there are 2 lines like
	IF PQL_MWSDEFAULT .LT. WSMAX THEN PQL_MWSDEFAULT = WSMAX
	IF PQL_MWSEXTENT .LT. WSMAX THEN PQL_MWSEXTENT = WSMAX
In both lines the ".LT." must be changed to ".GT."
I believe in version VMS 7.1 this is fixed.

If you type in at DCL: $ SHOW WORK
you can easily see if the WSEXTENT is as high as WSMAX.

By the way: At the moment i donot have connection to a VAX system so i am 
typing al this by heart. SO there could be things misspelled.




