I looked at OpenVMS VAX V6.2 and found the relevent section at LINE 2780

$param_name = "PQL_DWSEXTENT"
$Gosub Get_Param_Limits
$temp = pql_dwsdefault * 2
$IF MMG_CTLFLAGS .NE. 0
$THEN
$IF temp .LT. WSMAX then temp = WSMAX               !**** CHANGE .LT. to .GT.
$ENDIF
$GOSUB Check_overrides
$IF temp .NE. pql_dwsextent THEN GOSUB output_overrides
$param_name = "PQL_MWSEXTENT"
$Gosub Get_Param_Limits
$temp = pql_mwsdefault * 2
$IF MMG_CTLFLAGS .NE. 0
$THEN
$IF temp .LT. WSMAX then temp = WSMAX               !**** CHANGE .LT. to .GT.
$ENDIF
$GOSUB Check_overrides
$IF temp .NE. pql_mwsextent THEN GOSUB output_overrides


I Wonder If there is a reason for this. I see this is only done if
MMG_CTLFLAGS is not 0. i.e. proactive memory reclaimation is enabled.

Can any DECbody say if this is deliberate or a bug ?

