DIGITAL Visual Fortran isn't a VMS product, so it isn't typically discussed
here.  comp.lang.fortran is more appropriate.  I'm working on a FAQ, but
you'll find lots of information already at http://www.digital.com/fortran

DIGITAL Visual Fortran doesn't provide any library of "VMS emulation"
routines - Windows NT is *NOT* OpenVMS!  However, Sector7 has a product
called VX/RT which claims to provide many such routines - I have not yet
had the chance to try it myself.  www.sector7.com.

The DVF documentation does not discuss migrating OpenVMS system service
and RTL calls to Windows APIs.
